%S A395859 0,0,0,11,111,79,7052
%N A395859 Number of enantiomorphic pairs among n-dimensional space groups.
%C A395859 7045 <= a(6) <= 7052.
%C A395859 a(6) = 7052, computed for all 85308 arithmetic classes of the corrected CARAT tables, with the cohomology H^1(G, Q^6/Z^6) and the normalizer action computed independently of CARAT. - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Oct 05 2026
%H A395859 Bachir Bekka and Christian Brouder, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.22265">Representations of the symmetry groups of infinite crystals</a>, arXiv:2512.22265 [cond-mat.mtrl-sci], 2025.
%H A395859 Franka Miriam Brückler and Vladimir Stilinović, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-19071-2_132-2">From Friezes to Quasicrystals: A History of Symmetry Groups</a>, 2023, in: Handbook of the History and Philosophy of Mathematical Practice, Springer.
%H A395859 B. Souvignier, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1107/S0108767303004161">Enantiomorphism of crystallographic groups in higher dimensions with results in dimensions up to 6</a>, Acta Cryst., A59 (2003), 210-220.
%F A395859 a(n) = A006227(n) - A004029(n).
%Y A395859 Cf. A006227, A004029.
